<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02C2">Remark <span data-tag="02C2">4.5.1.26</span>.</a> Let $\mathbf{Cat}$ denote the (strict) bicategory of categories (see Example <a data-tag="007M" href="/tag/007M">2.2.0.4</a>). The construction $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\mapsto \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ defines an isomorphism from $\mathbf{Cat}$ to the full subcategory of $\operatorname {h}_{2} \mathit{\operatorname{\mathbf{QCat}}}$ spanned by those objects of the form $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$, where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a (small) category. </p>
